69711926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gsT02","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T18:53:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T18:54:24Z","body":"> Do you have a sense of why this has become more of an issue in the new version of SSR? I guess because the spikiness ends up polluting the mip maps more?\r\n\r\nIn the new SSR, ray bias is applied by comparing how much the normal mapped normal deviates from the geometric normal. With the spiky depth buffer, the geometric normals also become spiky and the ray bias goes all over the place.\r\n\r\nRelevant code: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/effects/screen_space_reflection.glsl#L131","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3769711926/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_gith